# DTF tier manifest: conda-package-304
#   (artifact-keeper#4579 conditional package downloads, #4181 one-statement
#    package route; 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-conda (the conda-channel-
# types tier's stdlib-python static conda channel on 172.16.<slot>.70; it
# serves the real package dtfup-alpha-2.0-0.tar.bz2 in noarch and logs every
# request line to stdout).
#
# THE BUG
# #4579  Conda package downloads ignored If-None-Match and If-Modified-Since
#        and carried no ETag or Last-Modified, so an artifact manager in front
#        of Artifact Keeper that revalidates its cache (Nexus in the #4579
#        walkthrough) re-downloaded every package on each refresh, while
#        repodata was correctly answered 304. Fixed: every package response
#        carries ETag "<sha256>" and Last-Modified, and a request whose
#        validator matches is 304 with no body, on a hosted channel, a cached
#        Remote, a Virtual (served by a hosted member and by a cached Remote
#        member), and under both token URL layouts.
#
# CONTROLS (pass on every image)
#   a hosted, a Remote and a Virtual package download is 200 with the right
#   bytes, with and without a stale validator.
#
# FIX CASES (RED on ak-backend:1.11.5: 200 with the full body, no ETag)
#   hosted / token layouts / virtual-over-hosted: ETag is the sha256, 304 on
#     If-None-Match (exact and W/ forms) and on If-Modified-Since.
#   cached Remote and virtual-over-cached-Remote: ETag is the sha256, 304 on
#     If-None-Match, and the mock sees no request for the package.
#   a quarantined hosted package is refused 409 even with a matching
#     validator (CONTROL on 1.11.5, where it is 409 too).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login then ~40 calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the remote's upstream is the mock on a
# private address.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
